1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,833
Three o'clock on a Tuesday afternoon,
on the mountain side of a town

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,000
on Maui, an engine crew pulls

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,840
up to a burning field and reports

4
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:07,740
what it can see.

5
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,580
A fire about twenty feet

6
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,580
by a hundred, moving toward the ocean.

7
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:13,320
It is the same field

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,057
they were called to that morning.

9
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:18,040
What nobody standing in it knows
is that the phones in the town

10
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,987
below them stopped working hours ago.

11
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,540
This is a story about a warning.

12
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,720
Not about whether one was sent,

13
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,640
because one was.

14
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,700
About what it was sent over,

15
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,520
and what it was sent by,

16
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,040
and which of the two the state

17
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:33,040
had actually built.

18
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,475
Over the next half hour you will hear
what the largest warning system

19
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:39,620
of its kind in the world was
actually for, what happened

20
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,730
in the town on the morning before the
fire that everyone remembers,

21
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,540
why the message that went out went

22
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,280
out at sixteen minutes past four,

23
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,600
and what the state's own investigators wrote

24
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,400
at the end of five hundred

25
00:00:50,401 --> 00:00:53,660
and eighteen pages. A warning system
is not the equipment you own.

26
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:54,760
It is the thing

27
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,339
you are in the habit of using.

28
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,660
Hawaiʻi has more outdoor warning sirens

29
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,239
than any other place on earth.

30
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:03,900
That is not a boast made

31
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:04,800
by an outsider.

32
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,320
It is the first line

33
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,720
of the state's own description

34
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:08,820
of the system.

35
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:11,860
"Hawaiʻi has the largest single integrated

36
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:14,260
Outdoor Siren Warning System
for Public Safety

37
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:15,160
in the world."

38
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,560
More than four hundred of them stand

39
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,594
on the islands.

40
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,489
About eighty of those are on Maui.

41
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:21,980
They are tested.

42
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,936
Not occasionally, and not after an incident.

43
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,580
On a schedule, in public,

44
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:29,020
in daylight, on the first business day

45
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:33,160
of every month, together with the emergency
broadcast system and the local radio

46
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,423
and television stations.

47
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,486
Which means that for decades,

48
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:37,851
on one morning a month,

49
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,240
everybody on those islands has heard exactly

50
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,766
what that system sounds like.

51
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,520
And the state publishes what

52
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,420
it is for.

53
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,180
The list is not short.

54
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,780
Tsunamis.

55
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:48,840
Hurricanes.

56
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,480
Dam breaches.

57
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,680
Flooding.

58
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:53,080
Wildfires.

59
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,680
Volcanic eruptions.

60
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,427
Terrorist threats.

61
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,666
Hazardous material incidents.

62
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,288
Wildfires are on the list.

63
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,640
They are on the list in the state's own words,
published on the state's own page,

64
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,460
before any of this happened.

65
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,220
There is one more thing

66
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:08,840
on that page,

67
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:11,060
and it is the part almost nobody

68
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:11,960
knows.

69
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,760
The sirens do not tell you what

70
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:14,660
to do.

71
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,971
They are not a message.

72
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:19,025
They are an instruction to
go and find the message.

73
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:20,700
The state's own guidance

74
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,020
is that if you hear a siren

75
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,300
tone at any time other

76
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,540
than a scheduled test,

77
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,949
you should tune in to local radio,

78
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:29,800
television or cable for
emergency information

79
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,800
and instructions from the authorities.

80
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,816
That is the whole design.

81
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,060
A sound that reaches everybody,

82
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,300
followed by a message that explains it.

83
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,500
Hold on to that,

84
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,740
because the second half

85
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,820
of it is going to matter
more than the first.

86
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,173
Now the week before.

87
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:48,980
On the first of August, twenty twenty-three,
the National Weather Service

88
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,840
issued a forecast discussion that predicted

89
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,480
stronger trade winds and dry air arriving

90
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,440
with the passage of a hurricane,

91
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,880
and mentioned the possibility of Red Flag

92
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:00,930
conditions by early the following week.

93
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,500
A Red Flag Warning is a statement

94
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,240
that the weather itself is now capable

95
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,740
of turning a small ignition

96
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,600
into a fire that cannot be caught.

97
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,562
The hurricane was called Dora, and
it never came near the islands.

98
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,960
It passed about five hundred miles

99
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:14,920
to the south.

100
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,165
What it did was pull.

101
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,560
The gap between its low pressure

102
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,140
and the high pressure to the north

103
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:21,520
squeezed the air between them,

104
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:23,080
and the wind that came out

105
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:24,160
of that gap was dry,

106
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,792
and it came down the mountains.

107
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:30,220
On the third of August, the forecast
discussion specifically mentioned

108
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,780
the possibility of severe
fire weather developing

109
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,096
early in the coming week.

110
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,020
That same period, a forecaster contacted

111
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:38,680
his fire contacts directly,

112
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,740
telling them to expect strong,

113
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:42,920
dry winds on the Monday and Tuesday,

114
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,260
and warning them that a Fire Weather

115
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,313
Watch would be issued over the weekend.

116
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,280
And the report records something about

117
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:51,480
that call that is worth saying slowly.

118
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:54,400
The forecaster recognised
that this much notice

119
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,821
of such a warning was rare.

120
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,220
On the fifth of August, the service
raised its level of concern

121
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,580
and predicted that Monday and Tuesday would

122
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,940
bring critical fire weather, with
Tuesday especially dry.

123
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:08,403
At thirty-three minutes past three
in the morning on the sixth

124
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,600
of August, Red Flag Warnings were issued

125
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,500
for the leeward portions of the Hawaiian

126
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,400
Islands.

127
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,208
Lahaina was named in them.

128
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:18,460
On the fourth of August, the forecast
office in Honolulu sent

129
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:19,780
a notice to state agencies,

130
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,280
including the state's emergency management

131
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:25,360
agency, about high winds
and impending critical

132
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,260
fire weather.

133
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:29,720
And early on the eighth of August, between
three in the morning and half

134
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:32,440
past nine, the service repeated its wind

135
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,980
and Red Flag warnings and predicted gusts

136
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,506
of up to sixty miles an hour.

137
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,340
So the forecast was right.

138
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:39,840
It was early.

139
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:42,005
And it named the place.

140
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,740
Which raises an obvious question,

141
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,700
and the state's own investigators answered

142
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:46,510
it.

143
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:50,720
Their sixth finding is that there is little
perceptible difference between Hawaiʻi's

144
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,060
Red Flag criteria and a typical summer

145
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:55,560
day, and that this may have contributed

146
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,360
to how the forecast was received.

147
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,960
In a place where the trade winds

148
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,180
blow most of the year

149
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,320
and the leeward side is dry most

150
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,440
of the year, the warning that says

151
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,500
today is dangerous looks a great deal

152
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,840
like the page that says today

153
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,740
is Tuesday.

154
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,060
And their eighth finding is about

155
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:13,534
where the numbers came from.

156
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,660
The fire weather forecasts and the Red

157
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:17,640
Flag Warnings were based on data collected

158
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,880
at the airport in Honolulu,

159
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,560
which is on a different island.

160
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,080
West Maui did not have the automated

161
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,840
weather stations that would have shown

162
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:27,180
where Red Flag conditions actually existed

163
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,080
on the ground.

164
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:31,160
So the warning that arrived was
correct, and it was general,

165
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,480
and it was assembled on another island.

166
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,180
The fires started before dawn,

167
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:38,654
and there was more than one.

168
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:40,860
At twenty-two minutes past midnight,

169
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,480
a fire began upcountry,

170
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,120
at Olinda, on the other side

171
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,020
of the island.

172
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,920
It grew quickly and it took days.

173
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,040
At thirty-four minutes past six

174
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,840
in the morning, on the mountain side

175
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,840
of Lahaina, a second fire started.

176
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,180
The origin and cause of that fire

177
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:56,127
are on the record,

178
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,300
they were published by the County
of Maui and the federal Bureau

179
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:02,600
of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms
and Explosives,

180
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,360
and they are not in dispute

181
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,260
in this film.

182
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:08,460
"At 6:34 a.m., the fire originated off

183
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,880
Lahainaluna Road in the unmaintained
vegetation

184
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,600
near utility pole 25 as a result

185
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:16,151
of molten metallic material —

186
00:06:16,152 --> 00:06:16,985
sparks —

187
00:06:16,986 --> 00:06:19,220
ejected from the re-energization of broken

188
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,220
power lines above."

189
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,160
Broken lines.

190
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,723
Power returning to them.

191
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,820
Metal melting and falling into grass

192
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,978
that had not been cut.

193
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,524
The fire chief said it in one sentence
at the news conference:

194
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:33,140
the origin and cause of the
Lahaina fire is clear.

195
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,397
The classification is Accidental.

196
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,820
Not incendiary, not natural,

197
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:38,925
and not undetermined.

198
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,580
That is the answer,

199
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,720
it was published in October of twenty

200
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,440
twenty-four, and this film will

201
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,885
not be raising it again.

202
00:06:45,886 --> 00:06:48,803
But something else had already happened
that morning, before the fire,

203
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:51,220
and it decided more than people realise.

204
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:56,900
The wind arrived across central and western
Maui in the early hours. Trees came down.

205
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,080
Utility poles came down.

206
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,682
Power lines came down across roads.

207
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,140
At twenty minutes to six

208
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:04,835
in the morning —

209
00:07:04,836 --> 00:07:06,836
nearly an hour before the fire started

210
00:07:06,902 --> 00:07:07,202
—

211
00:07:07,203 --> 00:07:09,828
the police were logging downed poles
and lines at Keawe Street,

212
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,900
on the northbound lanes of the highway.

213
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,440
That intersection is the one that carries
traffic north and south through Lahaina,

214
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,200
and it is how you reach

215
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,100
the bypass.

216
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:22,060
The log's own summary of the
effect is four words long.

217
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,933
Limited evacuation from south to north.

218
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,718
Before anything was burning in that town,

219
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,680
one of the ways out

220
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,504
of it was already narrower than
it had been the day before.

221
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:35,920
Two words are going to keep coming up, and they
are the two directions that matter here.

222
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,424
Mauka means toward the mountain.

223
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,201
Makai means toward the sea.

224
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,180
Lahaina sits on a slope between the two.

225
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:44,393
The fire came mauka.

226
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,719
Everything the town was built to
be warned about came makai.

227
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:49,760
The morning fire was fought hard,

228
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,220
by ground crews with private bulldozers

229
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:54,860
and water tankers, cutting perimeter lines

230
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,071
and soaking the ground.

231
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,700
It was contained before nine

232
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:58,600
in the morning.

233
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,380
And then, in the County's own words:

234
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,300
all available indicators showed the fire

235
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:05,304
was fully contained and extinguished.

236
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:06,520
No flames.

237
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,660
No smoke.

238
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,340
No perceptibly combusting material observed,

239
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:11,600
for several hours.

240
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:13,790
At ten to eight that morning,

241
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:16,400
the relieving crew walked the burned
ground and looked at it.

242
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,740
The officer noted that power lines had

243
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,620
already come down along the gulch behind

244
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:23,160
the houses, and that the lines still

245
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:25,397
standing were swaying in the wind.

246
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,250
At twenty-seven minutes past eleven,

247
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,730
a third fire started upcountry,

248
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,660
at Kula.

249
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,780
It burned uncontained for over a week.

250
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,740
There was a fourth on the
island that day as well.

251
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:38,600
Emergency responders on Maui
were not managing one fire.

252
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,200
They were managing four, and continuing
to take new calls across

253
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,100
the island.

254
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,790
And then, in the late morning,

255
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,136
the town lost its phones.

256
00:08:46,780 --> 00:08:48,727
The state's timeline puts it plainly.

257
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:52,122
High winds crippled the communications
infrastructure,

258
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:54,880
destroying cellular phone
communication within

259
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,840
the Lahaina region in the late morning

260
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,140
of August the eighth.

261
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,860
The report then spells out what

262
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,720
that meant, and it is worth hearing

263
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,620
all of it.

264
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,632
With no cellular communication,

265
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:08,034
residents and tourists were not able
to receive emergency alerts,

266
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:11,960
communicate with loved ones, or receive
incoming or outgoing calls

267
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,860
or texts.

268
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:15,207
Not able to receive emergency alerts.

269
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:19,680
That is the state's own sentence, about the late
morning, hours before the town burned.

270
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:21,696
The police lost them too.

271
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:26,940
Officers in Lahaina had no cellular capability
at all and worked the entire incident

272
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,572
on portable and vehicle radios.

273
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,200
There were once landlines in houses
for exactly this reason.

274
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,840
Most households no longer have them,

275
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,620
and the report says it does

276
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:38,520
not know whether the ones that remained

277
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:41,030
were even working once the power went out.

278
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:42,920
At ten to one in the afternoon,

279
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,460
a county entry logged network issues

280
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:47,527
at Lahaina locations —

281
00:09:47,528 --> 00:09:49,423
the senior centre, the fire station.

282
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:51,360
At thirteen minutes past one,

283
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:54,080
the shelter at the Lahaina Recreation Center

284
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,160
reported that it had nobody in it.

285
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,314
Shelter population now zero.

286
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:01,622
At two o'clock, the shelter at the
Lahaina Civic Center closed.

287
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,680
At seventeen minutes past two

288
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:05,440
in the afternoon, the crews

289
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:07,680
on the morning fire reported it extinguished

290
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:08,996
and returned to quarters.

291
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:12,385
Thirty-eight minutes.

292
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:14,500
That is the distance between the crews

293
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,000
reporting the morning fire out

294
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,080
and the same ground being reported

295
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,980
on fire again.

296
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,500
Here is how the County described what

297
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,420
happened in between,

298
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:24,180
and this is the whole of it.

299
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:29,320
Despite diligent monitoring of the fire scene
and deployment of significant resources,

300
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:32,880
embers from the morning phase of
the fire remained undetected

301
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:35,080
and were rekindled by a severe wind

302
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,520
event at approximately two fifty-two

303
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,642
in the afternoon.

304
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:42,000
The County has been explicit about
the firefighters, and it said

305
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,660
so at the same news conference.

306
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:47,600
Its assistant chief said they wanted to
make abundantly clear to the community

307
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,840
that their firefighters
went above and beyond

308
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,960
their due diligence to be as confident

309
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,000
as they could be that the fire

310
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,140
was completely extinguished before they left

311
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,040
the scene.

312
00:10:57,200 --> 00:11:01,060
And the state's investigators reached the
finding that sits underneath that.

313
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,320
Their sixty-seventh finding
is that the firefighters

314
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:06,880
performed mopup as proven successful under

315
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,214
typical weather conditions —

316
00:11:08,215 --> 00:11:10,800
and that under the severe conditions

317
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,780
of that day, this level of mopup

318
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,749
appears to have been insufficient.

319
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,700
Mopup is the work of turning over

320
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,320
a burned area and drowning what

321
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,380
is still hot in it.

322
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:22,380
It is a procedure, and it has a standard,

323
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:23,660
and the standard was the one

324
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:24,560
that works.

325
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:25,833
That is the finding.

326
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:28,020
Not that anybody left early.

327
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:30,200
That the method that has always

328
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,640
been enough was not enough

329
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,540
in that wind.

330
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,789
At five to three in the afternoon,

331
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,140
the fire was reported again,

332
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:37,720
at the same place,

333
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,900
after numerous callers to 911 said

334
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:40,900
it was moving fast.

335
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,640
At two minutes to three,

336
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:45,160
Engine 11 reported it could see smoke.

337
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:48,000
At three o'clock, Engine 11 arrived

338
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,320
and reported the fire was
approximately twenty

339
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,220
feet by a hundred feet,

340
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:54,000
moving rapidly makai —

341
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,109
toward the ocean.

342
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:57,140
Twenty by a hundred is a fire

343
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,370
you can walk the length of.

344
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,420
At five past three,

345
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,320
police arriving at a shed confirmed

346
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,840
the first structure on fire.

347
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:07,039
Here is the mechanism, because everything
that follows is this repeated.

348
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:10,340
Fire moves through a built area three ways:

349
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,360
direct flame contact, radiant heat,

350
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,260
and embers.

351
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,700
Embers are made by whatever is burning
and carried by the wind,

352
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:18,920
and they start new fires beyond

353
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:20,183
the edge of the old one.

354
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:23,895
They get into buildings through vents, through
windows, through openings the wind

355
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:25,354
has already made —

356
00:12:25,355 --> 00:12:27,740
and the building burns from the inside out.

357
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:29,110
At twenty-one past three,

358
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:32,320
embers carried by the wind spotted
the fire across the bypass road.

359
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,461
At twenty-three past three,

360
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:37,440
command advised that the fire had
crossed Lahainaluna Road,

361
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:39,020
that it was in the park,

362
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:41,380
and that visibility was very poor because

363
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:42,591
of the amount of smoke.

364
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,581
At twenty-eight past three,

365
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:48,440
a ladder company reported a structure
on fire south of Lahainaluna Road.

366
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,180
At half past three,

367
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:54,660
vehicles were burning near the bypass, and
embers were reaching every house west

368
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:55,818
and south of the park.

369
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:58,222
At thirty-seven minutes past three,

370
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:00,066
this went out over the radio.

371
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:03,280
"There is one house on Lahainaluna
that is fully going now.

372
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,740
We need to stop

373
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:05,640
it where you are.

374
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,880
That has to be the cutoff there,

375
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:09,538
that road back there."

376
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:14,230
The engine that answered said it might
be multiple houses. Command answered:

377
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:16,471
yeah, there are multiple structures going.

378
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:20,160
Thirty-seven minutes after the fire was
reported, the question on the radio

379
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,940
was no longer where to put water.

380
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,080
It was where the line was.

381
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:26,460
At forty-three minutes past three,

382
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:31,000
an officer reported the smoke at the highway
was getting, in his word, pretty bad.

383
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,340
Now the warnings.

384
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:35,080
The county sends emergency messages the way

385
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,448
most American counties do:

386
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,680
as Wireless Emergency Alerts,

387
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:42,660
the ones that arrive on a phone with
a tone and cannot be switched

388
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:43,560
off.

389
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,280
Its alert log for that day

390
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,800
is in the state's report,
and it begins early.

391
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:49,820
At nine minutes past four

392
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:51,700
in the morning, an evacuation order

393
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:53,140
for a subdivision at Kula.

394
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,300
At five o'clock, another one,

395
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,480
for a road at Kula.

396
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,503
At twenty-one past five,

397
00:13:58,660 --> 00:13:59,818
another, near Makawao.

398
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,020
Those are the upcountry fires,

399
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,700
and they went out in the dark,

400
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,580
hours before the sun came up.

401
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,320
At four minutes past four

402
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,893
in the afternoon —

403
00:14:08,894 --> 00:14:12,897
an hour and nine minutes after the
fire was reported at Lahaina —

404
00:14:12,898 --> 00:14:16,380
an evacuation order went out for
a subdivision. It was for Kula.

405
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,534
At eleven minutes past four,

406
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:22,640
command asked for the power to be cut, because
of the number of poles and wires down.

407
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:25,821
The dispatcher confirmed
it within the minute.

408
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,740
And at sixteen minutes past four

409
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:30,600
in the afternoon, the first evacuation order

410
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,340
in that log that names a Lahaina

411
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,900
neighbourhood was sent.

412
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,988
Kelawea Mauka Subdivision.

413
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:38,120
Evacuate your family and pets now,

414
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,380
do not delay.

415
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,065
Shelter is open at Lahaina Civic Center.

416
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,940
The shelter named in that message had

417
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:46,308
closed two hours and sixteen
minutes earlier.

418
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:50,740
And the message was sent to cellphones, in a
region where cellular phone communication

419
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:52,860
had been destroyed in the late morning.

420
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,200
The County's position is that it sent

421
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:57,300
at least fourteen alert messages that day,

422
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:00,060
and that all twenty-one cell towers serving

423
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,080
West Maui, including Lahaina,

424
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:04,028
experienced total failure.

425
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,980
It sued four carriers over

426
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,810
it in May of twenty twenty-four.

427
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:09,760
The next entry in that log naming

428
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:12,140
a Lahaina neighbourhood is
at forty-six minutes

429
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:13,298
past eight that night.

430
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,100
It says to evacuate north,

431
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,600
out of town, toward Kapalua.

432
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:19,122
At half past four in the afternoon,

433
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,760
the county's emergency operations centre

434
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:22,813
was fully activated.

435
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,260
It had been at partial activation since

436
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,049
nine o'clock the previous evening,

437
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:30,074
staffed by two people, opened
for the wind warning.

438
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:34,520
That agency's full strength was an administrator
and eight direct reports.

439
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:37,273
Two of them were unavailable that week.

440
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:40,580
The police department was working
normal daily staffing.

441
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,708
Holding the night shift over on the
morning of the eighth brought

442
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:45,760
the number of officers in Lahaina
town to thirteen.

443
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:47,127
Thirteen officers.

444
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,780
For a town, on a day

445
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:54,860
the forecast had been naming it for five
days. By nightfall the fire had crossed

446
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,660
the highway and burned all the way

447
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:57,713
to the ocean's edge.

448
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:00,900
When the County of Maui published
the origin and cause of it,

449
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:03,360
fourteen months later, it recorded

450
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,840
that the fire claimed at least

451
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,380
a hundred and two lives.

452
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:08,260
That is the last number

453
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,049
in this film that is about people.

454
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:12,100
Everything after it is about what

455
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:14,480
was already standing on that slope before

456
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,585
the eighth of August.

457
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,577
Because by three in the afternoon

458
00:16:17,660 --> 00:16:20,360
the fire was no longer the
only problem, and it had

459
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,400
not been for hours.

460
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:24,220
The report's summary is
that the conflagration

461
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,800
overwhelmed the town's limited
evacuation routes,

462
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,840
some of which were blocked by downed

463
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:31,000
utility poles and electrical lines.

464
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:35,460
Limited is the operative word, and the
investigators wrote three separate

465
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,580
findings about it.

466
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,360
Severe congestion due to parked cars along

467
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,060
neighbourhood streets hindered
evacuation and response.

468
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:45,300
Densely populated and narrow
roadways hindered

469
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,960
the movement of both the fire
department and the police.

470
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,560
Roadways and evacuation routes
were not adequately

471
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:54,200
maintained before August
the eighth to sustain

472
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,420
effective evacuation during a fire event.

473
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,860
And zoning in some areas of Lahaina

474
00:16:58,860 --> 00:17:02,820
was not commensurate with the modern built
environment, the environmental risks,

475
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,316
or the population growth.

476
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,945
At four minutes past seven that evening,

477
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:11,640
one of the streets running out of town became
impassable. Another had already gone.

478
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,020
The report counts what that left.

479
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:19,040
The potential evacuation exit routes from Front
Street were reduced from eight to six.

480
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:23,200
At about a quarter to five that afternoon,
an officer working the residential

481
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,020
streets found an access road blocked

482
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:25,860
by a metal gate,

483
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,480
and the gate was locked.

484
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,780
Behind it, by his count,

485
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:31,580
were thirty to fifty cars that could

486
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,480
not get out.

487
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,820
A resident brought a reciprocating saw

488
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:35,720
and cut the lock.

489
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,220
A chain-link gate nearby was pulled open

490
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,120
with a tow strap.

491
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:40,580
One side of it opened.

492
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:45,053
A driver stopped, because he was not sure
there was enough room to get through.

493
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,640
The officer looked at the buildings
next to the line of cars and saw

494
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,429
that they were now fully engulfed.

495
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:51,940
So he ran at the gate

496
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,240
and put his shoulder through

497
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,608
it to open the other side.

498
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:57,180
Thirty to fifty fully loaded cars went

499
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,127
through that gate.

500
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,380
One gate.

501
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:00,440
One officer.

502
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,960
And one saw that a resident happened

503
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:03,860
to own.

504
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:08,280
The state's investigators turned it into two
findings, and both of them are about

505
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:09,800
equipment nobody had.

506
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:13,060
Emergency responders did not
have ready capability

507
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:15,940
to unlock emergency gates
at various locations,

508
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:19,420
including schools, to facilitate
evacuations.

509
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:21,620
They were often forced to rely

510
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:23,094
on a third party for access.

511
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,880
Police officers encountered
barriers on roads

512
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:29,780
that could have been used as alternate escape
routes, and lacked the equipment

513
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:30,833
to get through them.

514
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:33,640
The recommendation asks for police vehicles

515
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,693
to carry kits able to remove chain-link

516
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,760
fences, gates and boulders.

517
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,380
A recommendation that a police car should

518
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:42,100
carry bolt cutters is the kind

519
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,960
of sentence that only gets written after

520
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,860
something.

521
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:46,900
Now the water, because the version

522
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,540
of this story that most people carry

523
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:50,560
is wrong, and the record says

524
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:51,460
so directly.

525
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,760
The common account is that the power

526
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,380
failed, the pumps stopped,

527
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:56,888
and the hydrants went dry.

528
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:02,300
The twenty-first finding of the state's
investigation is that no pumps are used outside

529
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:04,900
the water production facilities to provide

530
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,532
pressure in that system at all.

531
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,760
Both systems had uninterrupted
electrical power

532
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:12,300
during the August twenty twenty-three fires,

533
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:14,220
and produced water at capacity

534
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:15,976
for the duration of the fire.

535
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:17,353
Uninterrupted power.

536
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:18,840
Full capacity.

537
00:19:19,290 --> 00:19:20,200
For the duration.

538
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:24,900
What actually happened to the pressure is the
twenty-fourth finding, and it is worse,

539
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:26,111
because nothing failed.

540
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,840
As structures burned, the household plumbing

541
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,367
inside them failed —

542
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,508
plastic and other piping —

543
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,280
allowing unrestricted flow of water from one

544
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,820
or more locations in each home,

545
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:39,260
so that water flowed freely from more

546
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,140
and more structures, and the pressure

547
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,900
and flow in the fire area fell.

548
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,500
Every house that burned became an open

549
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,400
tap.

550
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,460
The system was not losing water because

551
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:49,360
it was broken.

552
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,160
It was losing water because

553
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,340
it was working, into a thousand holes.

554
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,860
The timeline records what that
felt like on the ground.

555
00:19:57,340 --> 00:20:01,340
Pressure in the mains dropped to the point that
there was no water coming from fire hydrants

556
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,656
in some parts of Lahaina.

557
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,660
A relief engine trying to refill found

558
00:20:05,660 --> 00:20:08,120
a hydrant producing, in the crew's word,

559
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,260
a trickle.

560
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,440
Another crew found good pressure and filled

561
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:12,409
their tanks —

562
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:13,680
down at the beach,

563
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,048
at the bottom of the hill.

564
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:17,162
By five past five the next morning,

565
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:20,380
the hydrants around the civic centre
and the fire station were dry.

566
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,180
And at half past three

567
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:23,710
on the afternoon of the eighth,

568
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:27,380
the system that tells the water department
how much water it has left stopped

569
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:28,280
reporting.

570
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,360
No storage tank data was recorded

571
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,676
for the rest of the fire.

572
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,539
Once that connection was lost,

573
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:35,880
the county's water department did not know

574
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,560
how much stored water was available

575
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,460
for firefighting.

576
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:41,860
The twenty-sixth finding states
the outcome plainly:

577
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:44,460
water was not provided with
sufficient volume

578
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:47,080
and sufficient pressure for
use in firefighting

579
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,448
for the entire fire event.

580
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:53,080
And the twentieth finding says the department
was seemingly in compliance with the water

581
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:55,200
system design standards for the State

582
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,100
of Hawaiʻi.

583
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,000
Both of those are true at once,

584
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,360
and the twenty-seventh finding explains why.

585
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:04,900
Water quality and cost make it impractical
to size a drinking water system

586
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,780
to meet the firefighting demand

587
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:08,148
of an urban conflagration.

588
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:10,360
A town's water system is built

589
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:12,040
to supply houses and to fight house

590
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:12,940
fires.

591
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:14,520
It is not built to fight

592
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:15,420
the town.

593
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:17,720
The same shape appears at the utility.

594
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,420
The thirtieth finding is
that Hawaiian Electric

595
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:22,320
did not have a Public Safety Power

596
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,600
Shut-Off program in place at the time

597
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,408
of the fire —

598
00:21:26,409 --> 00:21:29,820
the procedure, used elsewhere, of
switching lines off in advance

599
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:31,810
when the weather makes them dangerous.

600
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:35,480
The twenty-ninth is that a lack of utility
vegetation abatement regulation

601
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:38,540
and enforcement may have contributed
to vegetation

602
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,020
at the base of utility poles

603
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:42,000
and near transmission lines,

604
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,360
creating a receptive fuel source for arcing

605
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,260
electrical wires.

606
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:47,760
Receptive fuel source is the language

607
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,076
of an engineering report.

608
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:51,380
What it describes is dry grass

609
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:52,643
at the bottom of a pole.

610
00:21:53,260 --> 00:21:55,230
The twenty-eighth is that the utility,

611
00:21:55,260 --> 00:21:57,610
together with the fire and
police departments,

612
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,960
did not have an adequate staffing plan

613
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:02,065
for the wildfire conditions of that day.

614
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,931
And then there is the sixty-first finding,

615
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,035
which is not about equipment at all.

616
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,400
There appears to be a statewide culture

617
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:12,180
of dismissing and under-recognising wildfire

618
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,080
risk.

619
00:22:13,130 --> 00:22:15,972
The underfunding and under-addressing
of preparedness,

620
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:18,580
planning and mitigation
significantly impacts

621
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:20,500
all parts of the system and fire

622
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:21,400
outcomes.

623
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:25,968
And then the investigators added a sentence that
appears nowhere else in the eighty-four.

624
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:27,708
This cannot be overstated.

625
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,221
Three weeks after the fire,

626
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:35,791
the Attorney General of Hawaiʻi commissioned
an outside investigation of her own state.

627
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,900
She engaged the Fire Safety
Research Institute,

628
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:41,020
part of UL Research Institutes,

629
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,280
to conduct a comprehensive,

630
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:46,360
independent analysis assessing the policies

631
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:48,400
and performance of state and county agencies

632
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,740
in preparing for and responding

633
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:51,898
to the Maui wildfires.

634
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:53,988
Her own words at the time:

635
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,410
"I am committed to an independent,

636
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:58,660
unbiased, and transparent investigation

637
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:01,081
into the government actions
during the fires."

638
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:03,280
The first report came in April

639
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:04,745
of twenty twenty-four.

640
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:08,040
Three hundred and seventy-five pages,

641
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,800
and a minute-by-minute timeline built

642
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:12,140
from more than twelve thousand records,

643
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:15,120
covering the afternoon of the eighth through

644
00:23:15,121 --> 00:23:18,746
half past eight the next morning. It says of
itself that it does not analyse causation.

645
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,820
It only establishes what happened,

646
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:21,720
and when.

647
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,606
The second came in September.

648
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:26,283
Five hundred and eighteen pages.

649
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:30,440
Eighty-four findings and a hundred and forty

650
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:33,440
recommendations, drawn from an eight hundred

651
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:38,800
and fifty gigabyte evidence
database of body-camera

652
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:41,360
footage, dispatch audio, vehicle location
data, interviews and official documents.

653
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:45,085
Two of those eighty-four findings are the reason
this film exists. Finding thirty-seven.

654
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:47,840
Only one siren from the All-Hazard Outdoor

655
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:49,840
Warning Siren System was operable within

656
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:52,080
the burn perimeter of the Lahaina area

657
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:54,140
on August the eighth,

658
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:55,560
twenty twenty-three. One.

659
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:57,574
Inside the area that burned.

660
00:23:58,180 --> 00:24:00,930
Reporting at the time put the number
of sirens in the Lahaina area

661
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:03,020
at four, and described all four

662
00:24:03,020 --> 00:24:04,757
of them as sited along the shore.

663
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:07,470
Finding thirty-eight is a separate finding,

664
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:08,711
about a separate thing.

665
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:11,420
The All-Hazard Outdoor Warning Siren System

666
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:13,200
had not been utilised for warning

667
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,380
of wildland-urban interface fires prior

668
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:17,500
to August the eighth,

669
00:24:17,501 --> 00:24:19,160
twenty twenty-three. Not that day.

670
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:20,500
Ever.

671
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:24,027
In the whole life of the largest outdoor
warning network in the world,

672
00:24:24,220 --> 00:24:26,367
it had never once been used
to warn of a fire.

673
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,020
And it was not used

674
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:29,652
on the eighth of August either.

675
00:24:30,100 --> 00:24:33,350
Reporting at the time established that,
and the head of the county's emergency

676
00:24:33,260 --> 00:24:35,920
management agency confirmed
it publicly within

677
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:36,820
days.

678
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:38,840
At a news conference on the sixteenth

679
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:40,800
of August, twenty twenty-three,

680
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:43,898
he was asked whether he regretted
not activating them.

681
00:24:43,980 --> 00:24:45,401
His answer was three words.

682
00:24:45,660 --> 00:24:46,560
I do not.

683
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:48,591
And he gave his reason.

684
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:53,581
Had we sounded the sirens that night, we were
afraid that people would have gone mauka —

685
00:24:53,582 --> 00:24:54,830
toward the mountainside —

686
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:56,176
and if that was the case,

687
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:58,010
they would have gone into the fire.

688
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,356
He resigned the next day,

689
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:00,768
the seventeenth of August,

690
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,238
citing health reasons.

691
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:04,240
He has not been charged with any

692
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,140
offence.

693
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:07,240
The last recommendation attached to Finding

694
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,740
thirty-seven asks for a
statewide sustainable

695
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:12,240
programme for the outdoor warning system,

696
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:15,660
including functioning hardware
resilient against

697
00:25:15,660 --> 00:25:17,240
mass communications failure.

698
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:20,501
Resilient against mass communications
failure.

699
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,440
That phrase is in the recommendation because

700
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:25,880
of what the alternative turned out to be.

701
00:25:26,140 --> 00:25:30,900
The findings about the alerts that were sent
are just as flat. Finding thirty-six.

702
00:25:31,220 --> 00:25:32,940
Many residents did not receive a text

703
00:25:32,940 --> 00:25:36,435
notification from the county regarding
the high winds and high fire danger.

704
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:37,925
Finding seventy-five.

705
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:40,340
The alert systems in place did

706
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:42,600
not adequately inform residents of inherent

707
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:43,500
dangers.

708
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:47,778
Its first recommendation asks
for multiple alert systems —

709
00:25:47,779 --> 00:25:49,730
sirens, radio broadcasts, and door-to-door

710
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:50,807
notifications —

711
00:25:51,020 --> 00:25:53,080
especially when cell service and electrical

712
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,140
power are lost.

713
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:55,980
Door-to-door.

714
00:25:56,300 --> 00:25:58,440
That is the fallback the
recommendation reaches

715
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:00,400
for, and on the night itself

716
00:26:00,460 --> 00:26:01,513
it is what happened:

717
00:26:01,780 --> 00:26:04,600
an engine crew driving Wahikuli
at twenty-four

718
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:07,440
minutes past eleven, running
its vehicle sirens

719
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:08,598
and knocking on doors.

720
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:10,900
And Finding thirty-nine is the one

721
00:26:10,900 --> 00:26:12,163
that is hardest to read.

722
00:26:12,940 --> 00:26:14,993
Even when people were told to evacuate,

723
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,500
and conditions seemed obvious
that evacuation

724
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:19,840
was necessary, many refused,

725
00:26:19,840 --> 00:26:21,520
because there did not appear

726
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:23,940
to be official notification that danger

727
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:24,840
was imminent.

728
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:26,700
People were standing in it,

729
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:28,557
being told by other people to go,

730
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:31,120
and waiting for the thing that
says it is official.

731
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:33,733
There is one more thing in the first report,

732
00:26:33,780 --> 00:26:35,540
and it is four sentences long.

733
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:38,840
There is no data showing which emergency

734
00:26:38,840 --> 00:26:41,360
management personnel responded
on August the eighth.

735
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:42,900
The only missing sign-in sheet

736
00:26:42,900 --> 00:26:44,540
for the emergency operations centre

737
00:26:44,540 --> 00:26:46,280
is that agency's sheet,

738
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:47,180
for that day.

739
00:26:47,560 --> 00:26:49,280
The county has not produced it after

740
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,227
multiple requests.

741
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:52,820
The activity logs that would record

742
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:54,380
the response hour by hour

743
00:26:54,380 --> 00:26:56,560
were not received from that
agency's personnel

744
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:57,771
for those dates either.

745
00:26:58,220 --> 00:26:59,480
And so the report says,

746
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:00,580
in its own words,

747
00:27:01,100 --> 00:27:02,560
that because of missing data

748
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:04,460
it is difficult to make a complete

749
00:27:04,460 --> 00:27:07,040
and accurate accounting of activities within

750
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:09,480
the emergency operations centre from August

751
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:11,620
the seventh through August the ninth.

752
00:27:12,020 --> 00:27:13,910
The investigators had subpoena power,

753
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:14,840
and they used it.

754
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:17,880
One subpoena, served on
the county's emergency

755
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:21,360
management agency in October
of twenty twenty-three,

756
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:23,640
asked for all maintenance and testing logs

757
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:25,740
for the statewide alert and warning siren

758
00:27:25,740 --> 00:27:26,969
system in Maui County.

759
00:27:27,100 --> 00:27:27,920
They had to ask

760
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,025
for those in writing.

761
00:27:29,400 --> 00:27:30,980
The civil case has moved further

762
00:27:30,980 --> 00:27:31,980
than anything else.

763
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:35,420
A four billion, thirty-seven million dollar

764
00:27:35,420 --> 00:27:37,980
settlement resolving roughly four hundred

765
00:27:37,980 --> 00:27:40,688
and fifty lawsuits was announced in
August of twenty twenty-four.

766
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:42,480
In February of twenty twenty-six,

767
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:45,480
the Hawaiʻi Supreme Court ruled unanimously

768
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:47,585
that insurers could not intervene in it.

769
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:49,760
The first award determination notices went

770
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:51,392
out on the seventeenth of June,

771
00:27:51,540 --> 00:27:52,894
twenty twenty-six.

772
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:54,225
A notice is an offer,

773
00:27:54,340 --> 00:27:55,240
not a payment.

774
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:59,860
Nearly twenty-two thousand claimants have filed
more than ninety-four thousand claims.

775
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,820
As of August twenty twenty-six,

776
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:03,175
no payment has been made.

777
00:28:03,420 --> 00:28:04,500
An appeal over how much

778
00:28:04,500 --> 00:28:08,211
of the settlement the lawyers receive is
pending before the state Supreme Court,

779
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:10,083
and while it is pending,

780
00:28:10,220 --> 00:28:12,009
no settlement payment can be made.

781
00:28:12,420 --> 00:28:14,900
About one point one billion dollars

782
00:28:14,900 --> 00:28:17,581
is sitting in trust for the first
of four annual instalments.

783
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:20,620
So here is what the record holds.

784
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:22,740
A forecast that was right,

785
00:28:22,740 --> 00:28:25,020
five days early, and named the town.

786
00:28:25,820 --> 00:28:28,200
A warning that looked like an
ordinary summer Tuesday.

787
00:28:28,980 --> 00:28:30,840
Weather data from an airport on another

788
00:28:30,840 --> 00:28:31,740
island.

789
00:28:32,060 --> 00:28:34,300
Broken lines re-energised
over grass that had

790
00:28:34,300 --> 00:28:35,200
not been cut.

791
00:28:35,900 --> 00:28:38,321
Poles across the northbound
lanes before dawn.

792
00:28:38,700 --> 00:28:40,420
A fire put out by the method

793
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:42,620
that works, in weather the method

794
00:28:42,620 --> 00:28:43,720
was not built for.

795
00:28:44,420 --> 00:28:45,894
Phones gone by late morning.

796
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:48,720
An evacuation order at sixteen minutes past

797
00:28:48,720 --> 00:28:51,120
four, naming a shelter that had closed

798
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:53,080
at two, sent to a network

799
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,238
that had already died.

800
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:56,499
Eight ways out reduced to six.

801
00:28:56,900 --> 00:28:57,880
A padlocked gate.

802
00:28:58,580 --> 00:29:00,300
A water system in compliance,

803
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:03,374
bleeding out through a thousand
burning houses.

804
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:05,840
One siren operable inside
the burn perimeter,

805
00:29:05,840 --> 00:29:07,700
on a network that had never once

806
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:08,805
been used for a fire.

807
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:10,545
Eighty-four findings.

808
00:29:11,260 --> 00:29:13,408
A hundred and forty recommendations.

809
00:29:13,409 --> 00:29:14,920
And not one of them says

810
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,880
that sounding the siren would have changed

811
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:17,780
the outcome.

812
00:29:18,340 --> 00:29:19,603
That is not a loose end.

813
00:29:20,060 --> 00:29:21,113
That is the finding.

814
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:24,120
The report's own conclusion is a system

815
00:29:25,038 --> 00:29:25,338
—

816
00:29:25,339 --> 00:29:27,120
weather, fuel, building codes,

817
00:29:27,480 --> 00:29:29,694
roads, water, power and warning —

818
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:32,600
and a system is exactly what nobody

819
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:33,960
can be prosecuted for.

820
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:36,440
And there are things this film cannot

821
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:37,720
tell you, because

822
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:39,660
they are not in what has been published.

823
00:29:40,020 --> 00:29:41,260
How much of the town burned

824
00:29:41,260 --> 00:29:43,220
in acres, and how fast the wind

825
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:46,940
was actually blowing on that slope,
are not in the record we read,

826
00:29:46,940 --> 00:29:48,560
and we have not put a number

827
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,460
on them.

828
00:29:49,620 --> 00:29:51,600
Here is the part that is not about Maui.

829
00:29:52,180 --> 00:29:53,880
Every place you have ever lived has

830
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:54,800
a warning system.

831
00:29:55,440 --> 00:29:57,100
And every warning system is really

832
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:58,496
a habit —

833
00:29:58,497 --> 00:30:02,160
the one thing it gets used for, over
and over, until that becomes

834
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,318
the only thing anybody believes it means.

835
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:06,637
In Hawaiʻi the habit was the sea.

836
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,448
The equipment was general.

837
00:30:09,060 --> 00:30:11,271
Its own published list included wildfires.

838
00:30:11,700 --> 00:30:15,000
But the habit had one direction in
it, and the direction was makai,

839
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:18,589
and on the eighth of August the
fire came from the other side.

840
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:19,860
That has changed.

841
00:30:20,380 --> 00:30:24,860
As of the publication of the second report,
the county has implemented a process

842
00:30:24,860 --> 00:30:27,200
for activating the sirens for wildfires.

843
00:30:27,940 --> 00:30:29,060
So this is the ask,

844
00:30:29,060 --> 00:30:30,534
and it is not the usual one.

845
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:36,042
Find out what the warning where you live is
actually for. Not what you assume it means —

846
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:38,820
what the agency that owns it has

847
00:30:39,580 --> 00:30:43,288
published that it means, and what you are supposed
to do in the minute after you hear it.

848
00:30:42,620 --> 00:30:44,120
In Hawaiʻi the answer is one line

849
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:45,380
long, and it has

850
00:30:45,380 --> 00:30:47,680
been on a public page the whole time.

851
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:49,280
When you hear a siren tone

852
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:50,820
that is not a scheduled test,

853
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,187
turn on the radio.

854
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:54,444
The sound was never the message.

855
00:30:55,040 --> 00:30:56,440
It was the instruction to go

856
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:57,340
and find one.
